{
	title: 'Session data shape profile and generator',
	spec: "scripts/perf-profile <home> measures the shape of a hal2 home's session data and writes it as ASON: numbers only, no text from any session and no ids, names, paths, cwds or model names. It holds the count of sessions and of open tabs; history sizes in bytes (median, p90, p99, max) for open tabs and for all sessions; records per type; tool output sizes and assistant text sizes (median, p90, max); the share of outputs with code fences, lines over 1,000 columns, wide (East Asian or emoji) characters and ANSI escapes; images per MB of history and their sizes. tasks/<this task>/profile.ason is such a profile of the user's own data (run on an import by scripts/import-old, task 3q), reviewed by the user before it is committed; it is the only file taken from real data. scripts/perf-home <profile> <home> [--scale <f>] generates a home of that shape from filler text, deterministically from a seed: the same profile and seed give byte-identical files. --scale shrinks counts and sizes for quick runs. Generated histories are valid hal2 histories: they replay to provider messages, every tool call has its result, and they end idle. Tests: a profile of a generated home comes back within 10% of the profile it was made from on every number; perf-profile's output of a home seeded with a distinctive marker string in every text field does not contain the marker.",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['3q']
}
